<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Dividing a line internally</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A cable runs straight from the top of a mast at \(A({@A[1]@},\,{@A[2]@},\,{@A[3]@})\) to an anchor at \(B({@B[1]@},\,{@B[2]@},\,{@B[3]@})\) on a site in Kitui; coordinates are in metres. A marker P divides AB internally in the ratio \({@m@} : {@n@}\).</p><div>(a) \(\overrightarrow{AP} =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><div>(b) The position vector of P, \(\overrightarrow{OP} =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Go the right fraction of the way along AB, starting from A. \(\overrightarrow{AB} = \mathbf{b} - \mathbf{a} = {@vAB@}\).</p><p>(a) AP is \({@m@}\) parts out of \({@m+n@}\), so \(\overrightarrow{AP} = \dfrac{ {@m@} }{ {@m+n@} }\,\overrightarrow{AB} = {@tAP@}\).</p><p>(b) \(\overrightarrow{OP} = \overrightarrow{OA} + \overrightarrow{AP} = {@vA@} + {@tAP@} = {@tOP@}\), so P is \(({@tOP[1,1]@},\,{@tOP[2,1]@},\,{@tOP[3,1]@})\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_numeric(ex) := block([sx], sx: ev(ex, simp), if listofvars(ex) = [] and freeof(%i, sx) then "" else "Type a number in each box, not a letter.");
cv3(v) := matrix([v[1]],[v[2]],[v[3]]);
e1: matrix([1],[0],[0]); badm: matrix([q],[1],[2]);
/* Design: a point a given ratio of the way along a segment, a mast cable in Kitui. "Measured from B" (B - AP) is the same point as the swapped-ratio point, so one node covers both. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 4, Chapter 9, Section D, Example 2. */
dlist: [[[-5,-4,4],[-14,-7,7],1,2],[[-5,1,0],[-11,4,-6],2,1],[[3,4,-1],[-5,8,11],1,3],[[2,-1,-5],[14,3,-1],3,1],[[2,-2,5],[-8,-7,-10],2,3],[[0,1,-5],[-15,-4,0],3,2],[[-1,-2,2],[4,13,-8],1,4],[[-4,-4,-4],[-11,3,-11],3,4],[[-4,-3,5],[-9,7,-5],4,1],[[1,5,0],[15,12,-14],2,5]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
A: dlist[ix][1]; B: dlist[ix][2]; m: dlist[ix][3]; n: dlist[ix][4];
vA: cv3(A); vAB: cv3(B-A);
tAP: m/(m+n)*vAB; tOP: vA+tAP;
swp: n/(m+n)*vAB; frc: m/n*vAB; whl: vAB;
swP: vA+swp;
fAP: tAP+e1; fOP: vA+fAP; wOP: vA+whl;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
